{
  "description": "Exact-money contract shared by the Python (ab0t-quota) and Go (ab0t-quota-go) libraries. Identical copies live in both repositories; both test suites must pass every case. Amounts are exact decimals with at most 6 fractional digits (micro-units); |amount| <= 9007199254.740991 (2^53 - 1 micro-units). Canonical text has no exponent, no trailing fractional zeros and no '-0'. Computed costs (hourly rate x seconds / 3600, multiply then divide) round ROUND_UP to 6 places: away from zero, so any nonzero remainder beyond the 6th place adds exactly one micro-unit and an exact result is unchanged - the billing service's rule, the same as Python's Decimal.quantize(Decimal('0.000001'), rounding=ROUND_UP). 'error' is the refusal kind: syntax | precision | range.",
  "version": 2,
  "quantum": "0.000001",
  "rounding": "ROUND_UP",
  "max_abs_micros": 9007199254740991,
